hat's not  exact but that's a rough system of how  we built that and it provides a lot of  incentive to go get a high quality deck  to put in a bunch of time and play this  game and um to like battle your way into  into glory and riches you know because  there's so much money that players can  earn just by playing the game uh there's  there's actually reason to own these  assets and rent them to others so i have  i have players that will buy digital  assets not with the intent to play but  to rent out to other players and so now  across this entire economic spectrum  from the smallest minnow to the biggest  whale you know we have people that are  yeah i had i had folks send me a picture  of a bed and they said hey aggie this  game has changed my life i'm no longer  sleeping on the floor thanks so much  here's this beautiful bed and i've also  had people that have sent me pictures of  homes or cars and and all along the way  they're saying things like this game has  changed my life thanks so much and on  the upper end they usually end it with  please write tax software so that we can  figure out what to do with all these  earnings and so you know and that's  that's the dream to me the dream is not  you know just make it so that whales are  are bigger whales and it's not you can't  we're not going to run a game just by  like distributing money to the poor  there's got to be this entire ecosystem  that allows all participants that are uh  that are engaged in the game to do  better and i think i think that's where  we're at with splinter lands you can  learn more about splinterlands at  splinterlands.com we've been speaking  with the ceo jesse agro-dreich jesse  always appreciate your time and insights  and great to see you yeah it's good good  to be back thank you david and uh glad  to see your your channels are growing  and you're doing well
 

